  "notice": "Entry created successfully.",
  "entry": {
    "title": "v1 Retrieval Is Not Reasoning: Why Your AI Architecture Has a Context Gap",
    "url": "/blog/retrieval-is-not-reasoning-why-your-ai-architecture-has-a-context-gap",
    "lead_paragraph": {
      "type": "doc",
      "attrs": {},
      "uid": "708d8271dbae4b19a4fbb60320c63686",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": ""
        }
      ],
      "_version": 1
    },
    "content": [
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "9cd2136a529045229f9171fdd29078f8",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "h3",
                "uid": "a2ce0574dc4a413ebe3d941e9e39d5e6",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Quick Answer",
                    "attrs": {
                      "style": {
                        "color": "rgb(26, 78, 159)"
                      }
                    },
                    "bold": true,
                    "font-color": "#fa660f"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "ul",
                "uid": "1c33a84f6a0d4ccd8cde417838f02cca",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "a7ad7a56c6414d7389b13afb677be96a",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "e88204d5b9d646738df628dcf31b49d2",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Enterprise AI inconsistency is an architecture problem, not a prompt problem."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "f724c716248b44c4b19fe8038cf52b13",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "fea47ca7297a4ace9408853bfcf6654d",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Ontology, semantics, and knowledge graphs must operate as one semantic foundation."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "af1552a90fa343868abd5efbec65b0e2",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "3e28c1ac779e4048977e11d01027b8b4",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Without a shared semantic foundation, AI interprets terms like customer, revenue, and top performer differently on every query."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "74788da57101453c80b9e95400ee4fc3",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "0d879c3fd31c4d8db69054eac3aa5ea2",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "A semantic layer encodes business definitions once so every query returns the same reliable answer regardless of phrasing or model."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "4e891967a7fb47ddb460e801ef122ed8",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "b4e14e8810bc48ceb1fa3b290ed1955c",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Strategy Mosaic closes the context gap by sitting between your data and your AI systems, encoding business definitions as a persistent semantic layer so your AI doesn't retrieve — it reasons."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csc89e62fb3ad46583"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "1d7822251efa4970a5539f2ce2d4e101",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "4627ba368048453c84b7542ec8fd5f98",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "In enterprise AI, the challenge is no longer whether systems can respond, but whether they can respond ",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "consistently",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". The ",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "June 2026 Forrester Research report",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " ",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "\"Combine Semantics, Ontology, And Knowledge Graphs For AI-Ready Data\"",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " identifies the root cause of the problem: enterprises struggle to make data usable for agentic AI because data and data schemas still lack machine-readable meaning and context.",
                    "bold": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "e381d106e8874e7891fb56db5a424dd3",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Today's AI systems are remarkably effective at gathering context. They index vast stores of information, retrieve relevant fragments in milliseconds, and assemble them into responses that appear coherent and complete. Measured by access alone, the problem seems solved."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "21e787657f614f82abbd83b04b380b06",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "And yet, a gap remains. Between retrieved context and generated output lies an absence of shared interpretation: "
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "a missing layer that defines not just ",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "what",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " the data says, but what it ",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "means",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " across every use case. This is the context gap.",
                    "bold": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "blockquote",
                "uid": "a032795ffcdb4dc2a276749564b623fb",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "p",
                    "uid": "cfb12bde9f1540bdacaca3f412fe7820",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "\"No matter how well modeled, data without the context provided by shared semantics and mature ontologies will fall short for agentic AI use cases.\"",
                        "attrs": {
                          "style": {
                            "color": "rgb(0, 61, 91)"
                          }
                        }
                      },
                      {
                        "text": " — Forrester Research, Combine Semantics, Ontology, And Knowledge Graphs For AI-Ready Data, June 2026",
                        "bold": true,
                        "attrs": {
                          "style": {
                            "color": "rgb(26, 78, 159)"
                          }
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs0e038ce379be7d6d"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "Across AI Implementations, the Same Pattern Shows Up",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs144a489c935c31ed"
          },
          "section_id": "across-ai-implementations-the-same-pattern-shows-up"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "5f90b12852194b83b93b9f5a4dd29f03",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "ccb778d968de41bf8415f59ed48e9b77",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The symptoms usually look familiar:"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "ol",
                "uid": "93d316368bdd4a7598a80062d7a335be",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "88500f488cc8438a8e8c8d12a53c58c7",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "4265c15828bc4fa0bb43358263ebe150",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Plausible but wrong answers: responses that appear coherent but fail under closer review."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "044f44bf57b74faa976bc6fa958225d4",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "6367397feedd4143808a903069badaa8",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Inconsistent results: the same question returns different answers across runs."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "li",
                    "uid": "b27a9e1d5c71477f89dba891eafb15dc",
                    "attrs": {},
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "type": "p",
                        "uid": "098844f9fb834dbaad28cc9a31f741ce",
                        "attrs": {},
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Prompt-level workarounds: teams spend cycles engineering prompts instead of fixing the underlying outputs."
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "13d201fb547046509e72389ddc1330ee",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "This pattern is playing out inside enterprise data teams, where the instinct is often to fix reliability at the prompt level: adding more instructions, narrowing the scope, writing better system prompts, or hiring a prompt engineer."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "46a4233f65364eea85a3eb3d547b5548",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "These responses can help at the margins, but they do not solve the root problem."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs795662c97557fae5"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "section_anchor": {
          "header_text": "What is a Context Layer?",
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "cs3f8df08fa6cf8b88"
          },
          "section_id": "what-is-a-context-layer"
        }
      },
      {
        "text": {
          "text_content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "attrs": {},
            "uid": "54e9431fe2f441b8aaef4d1d4d45ef2e",
            "children": [
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "daba50562bf94eaeb08c331c214c3a4b",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Your AI might understand general terms like revenue, customer, risk, or performance. But it doesn't automatically know what those terms mean "
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "inside your organization",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "af1726ee32ca4c4581fbbe4d14a8c43b",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Consistency of response is only part of the problem",
                    "bold": true
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ". The deeper issue is whether the answer reflects approved definitions, established relationships, access rules, and the business context that governs it.",
                    "bold": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "668781eecb4c49bfa3c215a89199991b",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "When AI teams talk about \"adding context,\" they usually mean stuffing more information into the prompt. This can look like longer system instructions, schema documentation, or example queries that help at the margins but miss what enterprise data requires."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "71eab35d59c047d89b6ad492956f810f",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "According to Forrester Research, AI fails without context-rich data. No matter how well modeled, data without the context provided by shared semantics and mature ontologies will fall short for agentic AI use cases."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "6258b7d46b6940e8b70a50ecab67be50",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "What AI is missing when it fails on enterprise data is the conceptual map that your organization has built over years: what a \"customer\" means in your context (acquired? active? including subsidiaries?), which dimensions apply to which business units, what rules govern which data is trustworthy and which is stale."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "6ecd34f15e0f4b708d5255ddb3998c7e",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Enterprise AI needs a shared, machine-readable representation of the business, one that defines what exists, explains what it means, and connects it across systems."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "p",
                "uid": "c75a2c2d696d4eb2ba8476289333994b",
                "attrs": {},
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Forrester describes that foundation through three connected pillars: ontology, semantics, and knowledge graphs."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ],
            "_version": 1
          },
          "_metadata": {
            "uid": "csbc34005a68da1a7a"
          }
        }
      },
      {
